150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (In addition to the structure presented in the DECODE Competition Manual, the field contains one REPAIR ZONE per ALLIANCE: approximately 24 in. wide by 24 in. deep, infinitely tall volume bounded by intermittent ALLIANCE-specific tape and the adjoining FIELD perimeter situated on the OBELISK side of the FIELD. The REPAIR ZONE is an ALLIANCE-specific zone belonging to the ALLIANCE with the adjacent ALLIANCE AREA \(near the opposing ALLIANCE GOAL\). While the ROBOT is fully inside its ALLIANCE REPAIR ZONE, the DRIVE TEAM may power off the ROBOT using the power switch, remove it from the FIELD, perform repairs or adjustments in the ROBOT REPAIR AREA, and return the ROBOT to the REPAIR ZONE at any time during the TELEOP period. The ROBOT may be powered back on and re-enter the FIELD only from its ALLIANCE'S REPAIR ZONE. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
